   "what": "other-side"
  },
  {
   "note": "page 1 shows the louvre slits about 3 px apart along the strip, about 36 of them in a 110 px stretch. At about 1 px per mm that is a 3.0 mm pitch, good to about 0.4 mm. The slit is drawn 1.4 mm thick and 6.0 mm long, estimated from 12x crops as a fraction of the 48 mm depth. The small dot at the far end sits about 16.0 mm from the front and is about 1.6 mm across, estimated from one 8x crop.",
   "reason": "needs-photo",
   "scope": [
    "left",
    "right"
   ],
   "wanted": "a photograph of the lid taken square on, with a scale.",
   "what": "vent-slits"
  },
  {
   "note": "the data sheet prints \"48 x 1349 x 56 mm\" as W x H x D. That puts 48 on the front. Both pictures read the front face as 56. Page 2 reads the band 56.6 mm at 7.55 px per mm. Page 1 reads 56.0, 56.7 and 55.0 mm against the module and the two holes. A 48 mm front would make the module 36.7 mm wide, which page 2 does not show. The picture, not the label order, decides it. The front is drawn 56 wide and 48 deep, so both sheet figures are kept and only their assignment changes. No picture reads the 48 mm depth.",
