   "wanted": "the installation guide's port table.",
   "what": "port-labels"
  },
  {
   "note": "page 2 shows a black screen with a pale grey header, four white readout lines and 1/2. The shared display part draws a pale screen and carries no text. It is used as it is. Page 2 also prints Select and Enter on the two rings, and a dark surround and silver tongue on the USB jack. The ring names are not drawn. The USB part draws a silver ring and the blue tongue of USB 3.0, which the data sheet does not state. The two module screws are drawn as discs with an upright cross slot. The library part common/screw-head@1 is 3.6 mm and silver and takes no size, so it cannot draw the 5.6 mm dark screws. Page 2 shows the slot turned 45 degrees, which a decor box cannot draw. The `motif` pattern was considered. It is a vent pattern, its cells take a fixed dark, and it is not used for a slot.",
